From 39d42b6393f92c4a5bc4bf6d73877dcb83c7d257 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: localhost-copilot <318096335+localhost-copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:19:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: wave5: recover T7 encoders through a drained power
 cycle

Fail old M2M contexts before serializing a checked bus drain, dedicated-domain OFF/ON and cold firmware initialization. Require genpd notifications and a reset VCPU, retaining all DMA ownership if any stage fails. Keep old file handles failed and permit new contexts only after recovery.

Retain the probe firmware to avoid filesystem dependencies during recovery. Defer queue allocator releases and closed-context cleanup until recovery succeeds, balance close PM references, synchronize IRQ readers and expose one-shot recovery fault injection. Exercise production C recovery and ownership paths with deterministic fault models.

Signed-off-by: localhost-copilot <318096335+localhost-copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
